WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.931
Euclid's Elements, Book One, Proposition Forty-Six.

2
00:00:03.931 --> 00:00:06.547
Construct a square on a given segment.

3
00:00:06.547 --> 00:00:08.543
Let A B be the given segment.

4
00:00:08.543 --> 00:00:11.090
We construct a square on segment A B.

5
00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:20.323
From point A on segment A B, construct segment A C at right angles to A B, and cut off segment A D equal to segment A B.

6
00:00:20.323 --> 00:00:31.120
Through point D construct segment D E parallel to A B, and through point B construct segment B E parallel to A D, completing parallelogram A D E B.

7
00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:37.773
In parallelogram A D E B, opposite sides are equal: A B equals D E, and A D equals B E.

8
00:00:37.773 --> 00:00:47.588
Since A B was made equal to A D, all four sides B A, A D, D E, and E B are equal to one another, so parallelogram A D E B is equilateral.

9
00:00:47.588 --> 00:00:56.113
Furthermore, since transversal A D cuts parallels A B and D E, interior angles B A D and A D E sum to two right angles.

10
00:00:56.113 --> 00:01:10.656
Because angle B A D is a right angle, angle A D E is also a right angle; and since opposite angles of a parallelogram are equal, angles A B E and B E D are also right angles, making A D E B right-angled.

11
00:01:10.656 --> 00:01:19.540
Since figure A D E B is both equilateral and right-angled, it is a square constructed on segment A B, as was required to do.
